{
  "title": "Black Belt · Mockup E — refusals stay on screen in the amber bar (BB4)",
  "subtitle": "Drawn on the real preview screens (fake data, Spring 2027, admin). <b>What changes (rule v1.004):</b> when the database refuses something, Black Belt stops showing a toast that disappears after a few seconds. The words go in the <b>shared amber bar</b> (the one a failed save already uses) and stay until <b>×</b> closes it. Toasts stay only for “it's done”. A true refusal has <b>no Retry, only ×</b>: there is nothing to try again. A connection failure (“Couldn't save…”, “That didn't work. Check the connection…”) <b>always has Retry</b>, in the same bar. <b>One wording change:</b> the “someone else changed” refusal no longer says “Close and open them again” (nothing is open on a row, and the detail already shows the change). Now: “Someone else changed Rina Patel just now, so nothing was done. Their change is shown.” (inner green outline). <b>No question here.</b>",
