  "footer": "<b>The bar belongs to the tab it came from:</b> changing tabs or cycles clears it; a later successful action does <b>not</b> clear it; only × (or a Retry that works) does. One bar at a time: a new problem replaces the old one.<br><b>The same bar for the other refusals:</b> Restore: “Someone else changed Rina Patel just now, so nothing was done. Their change is shown.” and “Another make-up of Rina Patel is already on a cycle, so this one can’t be restored.” Delete permanently and the make-up's Undo: “Rina Patel has grades / payment records, so they can't be deleted. Withdraw them instead.” (inside the open Delete box these stay a note, as today). A refused toast Undo: “Couldn't undo. Someone else changed this candidate just now.” And “This candidate was deleted.” (in the Candidates tab's bar; the detail closes). The make-up picker's refusal comes from the toast's <b>Undo</b> after adding a make-up, when the picker is already closed, so it uses the Candidates tab's bar.<br><b>Connection failures get Retry, Undo's own included:</b> today the make-up's Undo (useMakeupPicker's undoAdd) shows “That didn't work. Check the connection, then try again.” as a toast with no Retry; it becomes the bar with Retry. <b>Toasts keep only “done”:</b> “Rina Patel withdrawn · Undo”, “Undone”, “Changes saved”."
}